    "description": "The Smart Exercise Cycle is a sustainable energy generation system that converts human mechanical energy into electrical energy during exercise. In conventional exercise cycles, the energy generated while pedaling is completely wasted. This project aims to utilize that energy productively by generating electricity and storing it for small-scale applications.\n\nThe system works by connecting a DC generator to the flywheel of the exercise cycle. When the user pedals, the generator produces electrical energy, which is regulated using a charge controller and stored in a rechargeable lithium-ion battery. The stored energy can be used for LED lighting and mobile charging.\n\nThe project also integrates ESP32, sensors, and a mobile application for real-time monitoring. Users can track voltage generated, RPM, calories burned, workout duration, and battery status through an LCD display and mobile app.\n\nThe main purpose of the project is to promote renewable energy awareness, reduce energy wastage, and encourage healthy lifestyles through a smart and eco-friendly fitness solution.",
