    "description": "The Case Delay Tracking System is a smart software solution designed to identify and monitor cases at risk of delay. Its primary goal is to enhance efficiency, reduce pending workloads, and ensure that sensitive or high-priority cases receive timely attention. The system evaluates key factors such as case duration, deadlines, priority level, and status updates to predict potential delays in advance. Once identified, at-risk cases are flagged, enabling authorities or team members to take immediate corrective action. This project supports better decision-making, increases transparency, and improves overall case management. Developed as an SIP minor project by a team of six members, it demonstrates the practical application of data management and tracking technologies to solve real-world organizational challenges. The system is highly adaptable and can be applied across various sectors including legal services, customer support, administration, and complaint management, making it a versatile tool for improving workflow efficiency and accountability in time-sensitive environments.",
    "end_users": "The intended end users of the Case Delay Tracking System include organizations and professionals managing time-sensitive cases or requests. Key users are legal departments, courts, government offices, customer support centers, administrative units, hospitals, and complaint management teams. Within these settings, managers, case handlers, administrators, and supervisors will directly benefit. They can monitor case progress, identify high-risk delayed cases, and prioritize urgent tasks efficiently. The system is especially valuable where delays impact productivity, service quality, or decision-making. By delivering timely alerts and structured tracking, it helps end users improve workflow management, reduce pending workloads, and ensure critical cases receive immediate attention. Ultimately, the system empowers teams to become more proactive rather than reactive, fostering accountability and transparency in case handling across various public and private sector environments."
