    "description": "This SIP project focuses on developing an affordable autonomous solar panel cleaning robot that operates without human control and uses zero water for cleaning. The robot is designed to automatically remove dust and dirt from solar panels using dry-cleaning mechanisms such as rotating brushes and automated movement systems. By maintaining clean panel surfaces, the system improves solar energy efficiency and reduces power loss caused by dust accumulation. The project aims to provide a cost-effective, eco-friendly, and low-maintenance solution for solar panel cleaning, especially in areas with limited water availability. This innovation supports sustainable energy generation and enhances the performance and lifespan of solar panels.",
