    "description": "Nutronics: Doctor-Verified Nutrition for Diagnosed Patients is a digital health platform focused on post-discharge care for patients with chronic conditions such as Type 2 diabetes. The project aims to solve a major healthcare gap where patients forget post-consultation instructions related to diet, daily activities, and warning signs. Nutronics provides doctor-verified daily diet guidance through a curated food database approved by medical professionals, ensuring safe and reliable nutrition recommendations. The platform acts as a 30-day recovery companion by helping patients follow prescribed dietary routines, monitor progress, and maintain healthier habits. Unlike generic fitness apps, Nutronics emphasizes medical verification, personalized care, and improved recovery outcomes.",
    "end_users": "The intended end users of Nutronics are patients with diagnosed medical conditions who require continuous dietary guidance after hospital visits or discharge. The primary target users are individuals suffering from chronic diseases such as Type 2 diabetes, cardiac conditions, hypertension, and obesity, where food habits directly affect recovery and long-term health outcomes. Many patients struggle to remember or follow doctor-prescribed diet instructions, daily activity recommendations, and warning signs after consultations. Nutronics is designed to support these patients with simple, personalized, and doctor-verified nutrition guidance."
