    "description": "A Smart Effluent Treatment Plant (Smart ETP) is an intelligent wastewater management system that combines modern treatment methods with automation and real-time monitoring technologies. Its main purpose is to treat industrial wastewater effectively before it is discharged into the environment, helping to control water pollution and protect natural water resources. The system uses advanced sensors to continuously monitor important parameters such as pH value, temperature, turbidity, and the presence of harmful chemicals. Based on the collected data, the treatment process is automatically adjusted to ensure better performance, reduced human effort, and efficient operation. The system can also generate instant alerts whenever contamination levels cross permissible limits. By enabling safe wastewater disposal and supporting water recycling and reuse, the Smart ETP contributes to environmental sustainability, cleaner surroundings, and responsible industrial practices.",
