    "description": "Feather Fence is a wireless System-on-Chip designed on an FPGA for smart agriculture that combines CNN-based processing with Linux, Python, and C to deliver real-time field monitoring, efficient wireless communication, and on-device intelligent decision-making. Built for speed, flexibility, and low power consumption in tough farm environments, it integrates sensors to track soil moisture, temperature, humidity, and pest activity, processes audio and image data locally through its CNN core, and wirelessly connects devices across the field to automate irrigation, trigger alerts, or adjust controls without cloud dependency. The FPGA platform ensures reliable, high-speed operation with reconfigurable hardware, while the software stack handles data logging, system integration, and adaptive responses. By merging VLSI design with AI-driven analytics, Feather Fence improves accuracy, productivity, and resource management, reduces manual labor and waste, and enables sustainable, data-driven farm management that helps farmers respond faster to changing conditions and optimize crop health.",
