    "description": "This project aims to improve healthcare services by addressing challenges in health insurance management and patient record handling. In many healthcare systems, patients face difficulties such as delayed insurance claim processing, lack of centralized medical records, data mismanagement, and inefficient communication between hospitals and insurance providers.\nThe proposed system focuses on creating an integrated platform that manages patient medical records digitally and simplifies the insurance verification and claim process. The system stores patient information securely, including medical history, diagnoses, treatments, prescriptions, and insurance details, enabling quick access for authorized healthcare providers.\nThe project also enhances coordination between patients, hospitals, and insurance companies by providing transparent claim tracking, faster approvals, and reduced paperwork. By digitizing records and streamlining insurance procedures, the system aims to improve healthcare accessibility, efficiency, and quality of patient care.\nObjectives\nTo maintain secure digital patient records.\nTo simplify and automate insurance claim processing.\nTo reduce paperwork and data redundancy.\nTo improve communication among patients, hospitals, and insurance providers.\nTo enhance healthcare efficiency and patient care quality.\nExpected Outcome\nThe project will provide a reliable healthcare management system that reduces administrative delays, improves patient data accessibility, and strengthens insurance support, ultimately contributing to better healthcare services",
