    "description": "Our project,  Sign Language to Voice/Text Conversion System, aims to help deaf and speech-impaired individuals communicate easily with others. The system detects sign language gestures using a camera and converts them into text and voice output in real time. This helps reduce communication barriers in places such as hospitals, schools, workplaces, public services, and daily conversations.\n\nThe project is designed as a simple and user-friendly solution that can work through a web application and can also be expanded into portable hardware devices in the future. The system uses Artificial Intelligence, Computer Vision, and Machine Learning technologies to recognize hand gestures accurately and provide fast communication support.\n\nKey features of the project include real-time gesture detection, text display, voice output, easy accessibility, and support for basic daily communication signs. The project focuses on creating an affordable, accessible, and socially impactful communication solution for the hearing-impaired community.",
    "end_users": "Deaf and speech-impaired individuals\nHospitals and healthcare centers\nSchools and colleges with inclusive education programs\nGovernment offices and public service centers\nPublic transport systems and railway stations\nNGOs working for hearing-impaired communities\nCustomer service centers and businesses\nFamilies and caretakers of deaf individuals\nEmergency response and support services\nRural communities with limited access to interpreters"
