    "description": "A Smart Fertilizer Management System using fertigation is an automated agricultural system that supplies fertilizers to crops through an irrigation system in a controlled and efficient manner. In this method, water and fertilizers are mixed together and delivered directly to the plant roots through drip irrigation or sprinkler systems.\nThe system uses sensors to monitor soil moisture, pH, temperature, and nutrient levels. A microcontroller or controller unit processes the data and automatically controls pumps and valves to provide the required amount of water and fertilizers at the correct time. This ensures that plants receive balanced nutrients according to their growth stage.\nUsing fertigation helps in reducing fertilizer wastage, saving water, improving nutrient absorption, and increasing crop yield. It also reduces manual labor and prevents over-fertilization, which can damage soil and pollute water sources. Farmers can monitor the system easily, and in advanced models, it can also be connected to mobile apps using IoT technology for real-time monitoring and control.",
