    "description": "The project aims to design and develop a smart rover-based silk crop cutting system that can move through agricultural fields and cut silk crops accurately without damaging nearby plants. The rover is equipped with cutting blades, sensors, wheels, a motor control unit, and a microcontroller to ensure smooth and precise operation. The system reduces manual labor, increases cutting efficiency, and improves crop safety during harvesting.\nThe rover works by detecting the crop position and controlling the cutting mechanism carefully while moving across the field. Sensors help maintain proper alignment and avoid unnecessary contact with healthy plants. The machine can be operated manually or semi-automatically, making it suitable for modern farming applications. This project supports smart agriculture by providing a low-cost, efficient, and eco-friendly harvesting solution for farmers.",
