    "description": "The Stray Dog Monitoring System is a smart technology project developed to monitor and manage stray dogs using a GPS-enabled smart collar. The collar helps track the real-time location of stray dogs and stores important information such as vaccination records, sterilization details, and health monitoring data.\nThe main aim of this project is to support animal welfare organizations ,NGO'  s ,Muncipal authorities and local authorities in controlling stray dog populations more effectively. By using GPS tracking, rescue teams can easily locate dogs for vaccination and sterilization programs. The stored data helps maintain proper records and avoid repeated treatments.\nThis system also helps reduce the spread of diseases such as rabies by ensuring timely vaccination of stray dogs. In addition, real-time tracking can help reduce road accidents caused by stray animals moving on busy roads. The smart collar provides a safe, efficient, and modern solution for stray dog management.",
