    "title": "Cold storage facility for farmers in rural areas",
    "guide": "",
    "dept": "Unknown",
    "students": [],
    "description": "Cold storage facilities are special storage systems used to preserve agricultural products such as fruits, vegetables, dairy products, flowers, meat, and fish at low temperatures. These facilities are very important for farmers in rural areas because they help reduce post-harvest losses and maintain the quality of crops for a longer period. In many villages, farmers are forced to sell their produce immediately after harvest due to the lack of proper storage. This often leads to low profits because market prices are usually lower during harvest season.\n\nCold storage facilities provide a solution by allowing farmers to store their produce safely until market demand and prices improve. These facilities use refrigeration systems to control temperature and humidity, which slows down the growth of bacteria and prevents spoilage. As a result, farmers can avoid wastage and earn better income by selling products at the right time.\n\nIn rural areas, cold storage facilities also support the transportation and distribution of perishable goods to distant markets without damage. They encourage farmers to grow high-value crops such as fruits and vegetables, which require proper storage. Additionally, cold storage creates employment opportunities in villages through maintenance, transportation, and management activities.\n\nGovernment schemes and cooperative societies often help establish cold storage units in rural regions by providing financial support and subsidies. Modern solar-powered cold storage systems are also becoming popular because they reduce electricity costs and are suitable for areas with limited power supply.\n\nOverall, cold storage facilities play a major role in improving farmers’ income, reducing food wastage, and strengthening the rural agricultural economy.",
